cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "TANDEM: Training-Free Joint Token and Bit-Width Allocation for Vision Transformers"
abstract: >-
  A theoretical model of end-to-end distortion for compressed Vision
  Transformers, D ~ sum_l S_l * eps_l, used to jointly allocate per-block
  bit-widths and token-merge budgets without any fine-tuning -- validated
  against published baselines (ToMe, RepQ-ViT, FQ-ViT) and on real Jetson
  Orin hardware (Orin Nano Super and Orin NX 8GB).
authors:
  - family-names: Sarim
    given-names: Muhammad Fawad Ul Hassan
repository-code: "https://github.com/fawadsarim/tandem"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords:
  - vision-transformers
  - model-compression
  - quantization
  - token-merging
  - efficient-inference
  - edge-ai
